cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Multivitamins: An Independent Evidence Review and Product Database"
message: "If you use this review, cite it as below. It has not been peer reviewed."
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Edwards
    given-names: Kevin
date-released: 2026-11-18
version: 1.0.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/tokyonocturn/multivitamin-evidence-review"
keywords:
  - multivitamin
  - dietary supplements
  - nutrition
  - evidence review
  - bioavailability
  - upper intake level
abstract: >-
  A source-linked review of multivitamin and multimineral supplements covering
  randomised evidence for mortality, cardiovascular disease, cancer, cognition,
  immunity, energy and pregnancy; ingredient forms and bioavailability; upper
  limits, toxicity and interactions; product quality and certification; and cost
  per daily serving across 20 products.
